        {
          "uuid": "64b018a1-a7b9-55cd-84b5-789d95cec853",
          "title": "Office macro security settings are enforced by policy and not user-writable",
          "description": "Verifies that macro security values live under the Policies hive and are GPO-delivered, which makes them read-only to a standard user. It does NOT prove a user cannot change them by other means: a local administrator, an MDM policy conflict, or a user with registry write access to the Policies key would still be able to, and none of that is visible from the value itself.",
